    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Moderate persistent asthma, well controlled with a recent exacerbation (J45.40)</content>. Asthma Control Test 21 and peak flow 590 L/min, so current control is good. The exacerbation six weeks ago is a risk factor for another, so stepping down now is not advised. Adherence and technique are good and the trigger was a viral cold, so stepping up is not needed either. He does not meet criteria for severe asthma or for a biologic. [S]<list><item>Continue budesonide-formoterol two inhalations twice daily and one as needed.</item><item>Action plan reviewed after the exacerbation; he will call on day two of any yellow-zone cold, and post-exacerbation reviews are now booked before he leaves the sick visit.</item><item>Reassess step-down at the next review if he has had no further exacerbation.</item><item>Influenza vaccine at next month&apos;s preventive visit.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Protocol monitoring: items the monitoring protocol calls for at this visit. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Measure</th><th>Interval</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Asthma Control Test</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>21, well controlled</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Peak flow</td><td>Daily or with symptoms for moderate to severe asthma</td><td>Completed today</td><td>590 L/min, green zone</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Inhaler technique with his own device</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Correct</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Adherence and reliever use</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Full adherence; reliever before training only</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Exacerbation history</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>One oral corticosteroid course since starting controller therapy, six weeks ago, with a viral cold; no emergency visits or hospital stays</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Clinic review within one week of an exacerbation</td><td>Within 1 week of any exacerbation</td><td>Deferred</td><td>Missed: advised at the sick visit but never booked, a deviation from the protocol; only the day-three nurse telephone check took place. No harm resulted: he recovered fully, and today&apos;s control and peak flow are good. Corrective action: post-exacerbation reviews are now booked at the sick visit before the patient leaves</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Written asthma action plan</td><td>Every visit and after every exacerbation</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Reviewed and updated after the exacerbation</td></tr><tr><td>Self-management</td><td>Trigger and exposure review, smoking and vaping status</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Viral colds remain his main trigger; never smoker</td></tr><tr><td>Survey</td><td>Step-up or step-down assessment</td><td>Every visit</td><td>Completed today</td><td>No change: step-down deferred because of the recent exacerbation; step-up not needed with good control, adherence, and technique</td></tr><tr><td>Examination</td><td>Spirometry</td><td>At diagnosis, 3 to 6 months after stabilization, then every 1 to 2 years</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Normal three months ago; next in one to two years</td></tr><tr><td>Referral</td><td>Biologic candidacy assessment</td><td>Only if severe and uncontrolled despite optimized Step 4 to 5 therapy</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>One exacerbation on controller therapy, with good control between; criteria for severe asthma not met</td></tr><tr><td>Medication safety</td><td>Vaccination status</td><td>Yearly</td><td>Due</td><td>Influenza vaccine planned at next month&apos;s preventive visit</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Goal progress:</paragraph><list><item>Asthma Control Test score of 20 or more by the three-month review. Outcome by 2026-06-08: ACT rose from 13 to 22 [S]</item><item>FEV1 of 80 percent predicted or more on spirometry after stabilization. Outcome by 2026-06-08: FEV1 89 percent predicted with a normal FEV1/FVC ratio [S]</item><item>No exacerbation needing oral corticosteroids over the six months after starting controller therapy. Outcome by 2026-09-14: Not met: one moderate exacerbation with a cold in August needed a five-day prednisone course; the goal continues for the next six months [S]</item><item>Return to full boxing and rowing training without limiting symptoms. Outcome by 2026-06-08: Training fully by the three-month review, using one reliever inhalation before sessions [S]</item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: Global Strategy for Asthma Management and Prevention, 2025 update (2025); 2020 Focused Updates to the Asthma Management Guidelines: A Report from the National Asthma Education and Prevention Program Coordinating Committee Expert Panel Working Group (2020); CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, asthma monograph (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit next month. Asthma review in three months, or within one week of any exacerbation. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-19: periodic adult preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
